  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Temperature difference of <math><msup><mrow><mn>120</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi></math> is maintained between two ends of a uniform rod <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> of length <math><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Another bent rod <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></math> of same cross-section as <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and length <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> is connected across <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> (See figure). In steady state, temperature difference between <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> will be close to:<br /><img height=\"139\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f4a72c42-4915-42fe-835c-5022aa111e48-image.png\" width=\"379\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
